---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/for/subscription-boxes';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'for/subscription-boxes');
const desc = description(site, 'for/subscription-boxes');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When should box previews send?",
    "answer": "Work backward from actual customization, skip and billing cutoffs. Use confirmed contents and give customers time to act; there is no universal lead time."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should every skip trigger a recovery series?",
    "answer": "No. Reflect the current state and volunteered reason. Keep service confirmation distinct from optional marketing and stop obsolete queued messages."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is month three always the churn risk?",
    "answer": "No. Analyze renewal opportunities by tenure, acquisition cohort and box type before choosing an intervention."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should the platform demonstration prove?",
    "answer": "That contract-specific state changes update eligibility before send, including multiple contracts, failed payments and gift expiry. A generic customer tag is insufficient evidence."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/for">All store types</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Subscription box email: coordinate previews, skips and renewal state</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">A box program needs email that reflects the current contract and the next shipment. Choose a platform by whether it can keep previews, customer changes and service notices consistent across each renewal cycle.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Build a contract-state map before a retention sequence</h2>
    <p>List active, skipped, paused, cancelled, payment-failed and gift-expired states with the source system and update timestamp. Separate customer identity, contract identity and shipment identity: one customer can own multiple subscriptions. Define what happens to queued messages when state changes and who resolves missing or stale events.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Preview before the real decision deadline</h2>
    <p>Plan item reveals around the actual billing, customization and skip cutoffs. State what is confirmed, what may vary and how to make a change. Book boxes can offer a spoiler-light preview and discussion material; snack boxes need product-specific ingredient and dietary information; craft kits need required equipment. Do not promise contents operations has not finalized.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Treat skip as a customer instruction</h2>
    <p>Confirm the change through the designated service workflow. For optional marketing follow-up, distinguish travel from excess stock or unsuitable curation when customers volunteer a reason. Do not automatically undo a skip or make a discount contingent on reopening a cancelled contract. A pause suggestion should explain its practical effect rather than obscure cancellation.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Find risk in your own cohorts</h2>
    <p>Use completed renewal opportunities and cancellation reasons to identify where retention changes. There is no universal third-month danger point established here. Separate tenure from calendar season, acquisition promotion and box type. Preview engagement can help diagnose content interest, but correlation does not establish that a preview prevented cancellation.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Keep giver and recipient communication separate</h2>
    <p>Record who paid, who receives the box, whether renewal is automatic and when the gift ends. Send payment and renewal details to the responsible payer and onboarding to the intended recipient under the merchant communication rules. Avoid revealing a surprise early. Do not convert a gift recipient into a promotional subscriber solely because they receive a box.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Demonstration brief and proposed contract rehearsal</h2>
    <p>Include Sequenzy as a candidate only if a demonstration can prove your subscription-app events reach the right contract. Proposed cases: two contracts under one email, skip just before send, pause then resume, failed payment then success, and a gift expiry. Check service-message ownership against actual configuration. These exercises have not been run for this guide.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Measure renewal opportunities rather than campaign credit</h2>
    <p>Track renewed contracts among those eligible to renew, voluntary cancellations separately from payment failure, skips later resumed, and support contacts about deadlines. Compare contribution after curation, shipping and incentive costs. A proposed preview experiment should preserve required service notices and customer controls; use the same renewal opportunity across groups.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Service ownership and evidence</h2>
    <p><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/fulfillment/setup/notifications">Shopify store notifications</a> documents event-based order, fulfillment, refund, exchange and account notices. Assign each service event a sender before adding marketing automation; this source does not verify any third-party integration. Reviewed 24 November 2026.</p>
    <p><a class="link" href="/apps">Tool catalog</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/replenishment">Replenishment workflow</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/product-launch">Product launch workflow</a></p>
  </div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
